What was built
- src/app/budget.mjs: price table (machine-local `prices`, versions in SQLite
  price_versions, none shipped), caps from workspace > repository > spec > task,
  key by key, with mode stop|warn. Fallback caps 2,000,000 tokens and 200 credits,
  set as workspace budget.tokens/credits. Spend priced on read (credits first).
  Batch caps are the sum of the members' caps, with turns shared evenly.
  Holds live in budget_holds; raises in budget_raises.
- Stop mode: the check runs after each usage read (app backend, under the tick
  lock) and in the tick before dispatch. It sends one stop message per live
  session, answers budget_reached on MCP calls except plans_report, and makes no
  verifier or review dispatch. Never closes a session. A budget stop costs no
  attempt.
- Warn mode: never stops or messages. Shows an Over budget badge and one Needs you
  item with Acknowledge / Raise budget / Switch to stop. The item reopens each
  further 50% of the cap. Notify is optional (budget.notify, off).
- 80% warning on the chip and receipt. The receipt shows any overrun.
- Intake grant (task.intakeBudget) fills only a missing dollar cap, always stop.
- Unknown spend (Crew Mode, remote, failed read) warns once, never stops.
- Person only (403 for MCP, sessions, app tokens): budget.raise, .stop,
  .acknowledge, .switchToStop, prices.save, budget.settings.update.
- Receipt: budget.receipt, `avoozl budget receipt TASK --json`, plans_view
  action receipt, retro payload `receipts`. Counts and dollars only.
- Refused by name: prices in .avoozl.json, in a pack, or in a manifest.
- UI: spend chip on Delivery cards and In flight, drawer Budget fold after Timing
  (tables, Export JSON, actions), Needs you items, Dashboard "N over budget",
  Flow bar marks, Settings > Budgets (mode with one plain line each) and
  Settings > Prices ("This computer only").

